      "extract": "Objects in algebraic geometry provide a rich source of symplectic and contact man- ifolds. Smooth projective varieties X \u001a CP N , for instance, have symplectic structures !X given by restricting the standard Fubini–Study form on CP N . Links of isolated singularities admit natural contact structures, given by a complex hyperplane distribution. What can such structures tell us about the underlying algebraic variety?",
